Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• Musical_Preferences.StyleID : musical style we are scoring (GROUP BY key)  
• Musical_Preferences.PreferenceSeq : tells whether the style was 1st, 2nd, or 3rd choice (drives 3/2/1 weighting)  
• Musical_Styles.StyleID : joins the numeric style id to its name  
• Musical_Styles.StyleName : readable name that we want to show in the result  

(Everything else in the schema is not needed for this task.)

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQLite SELECT statements.  
Each query is preceded by a brief comment and returns at most 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw preference rows
SELECT *
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. What distinct StyleIDs appear in preferences?
SELECT DISTINCT "StyleID"
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show the first‑choice (PreferenceSeq = 1) occurrences of each StyleID
SELECT "StyleID", COUNT(*) AS "FirstChoiceCount"
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
WHERE "PreferenceSeq" = 1
GROUP BY "StyleID"
ORDER BY "FirstChoiceCount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Second‑choice tallies (PreferenceSeq = 2)
SELECT "StyleID", COUNT(*) AS "SecondChoiceCount"
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
WHERE "PreferenceSeq" = 2
GROUP BY "StyleID"
ORDER BY "SecondChoiceCount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Third‑choice tallies (PreferenceSeq = 3)
SELECT "StyleID", COUNT(*) AS "ThirdChoiceCount"
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
WHERE "PreferenceSeq" = 3
GROUP BY "StyleID"
ORDER BY "ThirdChoiceCount" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Verify we can reach style names
SELECT ms."StyleID", ms."StyleName"
FROM "Musical_Styles" AS ms
ORDER BY ms."StyleID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Calculate each style’s total weighted score (3/2/1) without names yet
SELECT
  "StyleID",
  SUM(CASE "PreferenceSeq"
        WHEN 1 THEN 3
        WHEN 2 THEN 2
        WHEN 3 THEN 1
        ELSE 0
      END) AS "TotalWeightedScore"
FROM "Musical_Preferences"
GROUP BY "StyleID"
ORDER BY "TotalWeightedScore" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but attach the style names
SELECT
  mp."StyleID",
  ms."StyleName",
  SUM(CASE mp."PreferenceSeq"
        WHEN 1 THEN 3
        WHEN 2 THEN 2
        WHEN 3 THEN 1
      END) AS "TotalWeightedScore"
FROM "Musical_Preferences" AS mp
JOIN "Musical_Styles"      AS ms ON ms."StyleID" = mp."StyleID"
GROUP BY mp."StyleID", ms."StyleName"
ORDER BY "TotalWeightedScore" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compute the overall average of those total weighted scores
WITH scores AS (
  SELECT "StyleID",
         SUM(CASE "PreferenceSeq"
               WHEN 1 THEN 3
               WHEN 2 THEN 2
               WHEN 3 THEN 1
             END) AS "TotalWeightedScore"
  FROM "Musical_Preferences"
  GROUP BY "StyleID"
)
SELECT AVG("TotalWeightedScore") AS "AvgTotalWeightedScore"
FROM scores;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: total weighted score per style and its absolute
--     difference from the average score of all ranked styles
WITH weights AS (
  SELECT
    "StyleID",
    SUM(CASE "PreferenceSeq"
          WHEN 1 THEN 3
          WHEN 2 THEN 2
          WHEN 3 THEN 1
        END) AS "TotalWeightedScore"
  FROM "Musical_Preferences"
  GROUP BY "StyleID"
),
avg_score AS (
  SELECT AVG("TotalWeightedScore") AS "AvgScore"
  FROM weights
)
SELECT
  w."StyleID",
  ms."StyleName",
  w."TotalWeightedScore",
  ABS(w."TotalWeightedScore" - a."AvgScore") AS "AbsDifferenceFromAvg"
FROM weights          AS w
JOIN avg_score        AS a      -- Cartesian join to pull the single avg row
JOIN "Musical_Styles" AS ms ON ms."StyleID" = w."StyleID"
ORDER BY w."TotalWeightedScore" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Running Query 10 yields, for every style ever ranked, its weighted score and how far that score sits from the overall average of all such styles.
